{"term":"mortify","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:e3c2f06378b5374b9c","definition":"To discipline (one's body, appetites etc.) by suppressing desires; to practise abstinence on.","example":"Some people seek sainthood by mortifying the body.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["macerate"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["mortification"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mortify#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:83e8f14fcc3fefae6c","definition":"To injure the dignity of; to embarrass; to humiliate.","example":"I was so mortified I could have died right there; instead I fainted, but I swore I'd never let that happen to me again.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["demean","humiliate","shame"],"antonyms":["dignify","honor"],"collocations":[],"usage":"usually","register":"transitive, usually","wordFamily":["mortification"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mortify#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:62ad4ad073c60bd04e","definition":"To kill.","example":"The second Spring after transplanting, purge them of all superfluous shoots and scions, reserving only the most towardly for the future stem; this to be done yearly, as long as they continue in the nursery; and if of the principal stem so left, the frost mortifie any part, cut it off [...]","pos":"verb","synonyms":["dispose of","terminate","annihilate","bag","baptize","bereave of life","blight","bring down","bump off","bury","cack","compromised to a permanent end","croak","crush","dash","deactivate","dead","demolish","destroy","dispatch","dispose of","do","do in","dust","eliminate","end","eradicate","ex","exterminate","finish","finish off","flatten","grease","knock off","lay waste to","make away with","merc","mortify","neutralize","obliterate","off","pay off","pick off","polish off","pop off","punch someone's ticket","put an end to","put down","put someone out of their misery","put six feet under","put to sleep","ravage","rub out","ruin","scotch","scupper","scuttle","send to eternity","send to hell","send to the grave","send to the great beyond","send to the next life","shut up","slay","slaughter","slime out","smash","smite","snuff","squash","stiff","stop someone's clock","take","terminate","terminate with extreme prejudice","top off","top","torpedo","take care of","take down","take out","waste","wax","wet","whack","wipe out","wreck"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["mortification"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mortify#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4400b58aa0ceb1e34f","definition":"To reduce the potency of; to nullify; to deaden, neutralize.","example":"Soothly, the gode werkes, that he dide biforn that he fil in sinne, been al mortified and astoned and dulled by the ofte sinning.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["abate","cancel out","diminish","weaken"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["mortification"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mortify#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e7f925da64bf086bf2","definition":"To affect with vexation or chagrin.","example":"He seemed to enjoy mortifying them with news of every fresh hell loosed in the capital.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["disturb","perturb","agitate","freak","sting","bother","bring down","discompose","unstring","disconcert","enturbulate","disturb","mortify","perturb","put out","ruffle","throw off balance","unsettle","upset","flurry"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["mortification"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mortify#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5a2bc94d7b4f6a331e","definition":"To scare.","example":"Near-synonym: petrify","pos":"verb","synonyms":["frighten","alarm","affright","appall","dismay","fray","frighten","grill","give someone the shits","harrow","horrify","make someone's blood run cold","mortify","petrify","scare","scare straight","scare the bejeebers out of","scare the hell out of","scare the pants off of","scare the shit out of","terrorize","terrify","spook","petrify"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["mortification"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mortify#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:83d09fea32e719194b","definition":"To humble; to depress.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["mortification"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mortify#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c39af597d2ebb9f2b2","definition":"To grant in mortmain.","example":"the schoolmasters of Ayr were paid out of the mills mortified by Queen Mary","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"historical","register":"historical, transitive","wordFamily":["mortification"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mortify#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2d82f8f15f4f37a02c","definition":"To lose vitality.","example":"[...] Tis a pure ill-natur'd ſatisfaction to ſee one that was a beauty unfortunately move with the ſame languor, and ſoftneſs of behaviour, that once was charming in her—To ſee, I ſay, her mortify that us'd to kill [...]","pos":"verb","synonyms":["darken","die","fade","wither"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["mortification"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mortify#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3a45611d852f44040b","definition":"To kill off (living tissue etc.); to make necrotic.","example":"Servius the Grammarian being troubled with the gowt, found no better meanes to be rid of it, than to apply poison to mortifie [translating tuer] his legs.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["fester","necrotize","rankle","rot","sphacelate","decay"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic, transitive","wordFamily":["mortification"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mortify#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:30364f0be4358c90f4","definition":"To gangrene.","example":"For the inducing of putrefaction, it were good to try it with flesh or fish exposed to the moonbeams; and again exposed to the air when the moon shineth not, for the like time: to see whether will corrupt sooner: and try it also with capon, or some other fowl, laid abroad, to see whether it will mortify and become tender sooner; try it also with dead flies, or dead worms, having a little water cast upon them, to see whether will putrefy sooner.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["fester","putrefy"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic, intransitive","wordFamily":["mortification"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mortify#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d66df15c53bb8a7b46","definition":"To be subdued.","example":"Trying to be kind and honest will require all his thoughts; a mortified appetite is never a wise companion; in so far as he has had to mortify an appetite, he will still be the worse man; and of such an one a great deal of cheerfulness will be required in judging life, and a great deal of humility in judging others.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["abate","diminish","quell","subside","wane"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["mortification"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mortify#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/ˈmɔːtɪfaɪ/"},"wordFamily":["mortification"]}